.SH DESCRIPTION
Frees a breakpoint array returned by
\f[CR]bc_debug_list_breakpoints()\f[R].
For each element in the array, the function frees the heap\-allocated
string fields (\f[CR]kind\f[R], \f[CR]pattern\f[R],
\f[CR]condition\f[R]), then frees the array itself.
.PP
It is safe to call this function with \f[CR]bps\f[R] set to NULL (the
function is a no\-op in that case), which handles the empty breakpoint
list case from \f[CR]bc_debug_list_breakpoints()\f[R].
.PP
The function does \f[B]not\f[R] set the caller\(cqs pointer to NULL; the
caller should do so explicitly if needed.
